# Thinking Guides

## Scope

Shared project-wide workflow rules used by all packages and layers.

## Pre-Development Checklist

- Read `.superwork/workflow.md`
- Read the relevant package/layer `index.md`
- Choose `superwork-debugging` for bug work
- Choose light / medium / heavy for non-bug work by the shortest path that still meets quality requirements
- Choose `superwork-tdd` for light work; keep the TDD plan inline and do not require `.superwork/plans/*.md`
- Choose `superwork-writing-plans` then `superwork-executing-plans` for medium work
- Choose `superwork-brainstorming` then `superwork-writing-plans` then `superwork-executing-plans` as the default heavy-work path
- Allow manual `superwork-brainstorming` use on other non-bug tasks when extra design work is useful
- Reserve `superwork-code-simplifier` for behavior-preserving cleanup after the change is already green, and let `superwork-check` decide whether it must run

## Verification Checklist

- Run fresh verification before any completion claim
- follow `superwork-check` before final completion: that stage owns the `superwork-code-simplifier` decision, must run `superwork-code-simplifier` for medium or large diffs, and must state why when the current diff is truly small enough to skip it
- Use project-local commands such as:
{{ test_hints }}

## Update Triggers

- A new cross-package rule was introduced
- A repeated bug pattern needs durable guidance
- A verification requirement now applies across the project
